## 2. OUTPUT: dashboard (month by month, full year)
====================================================================

One page, top to bottom, shared X axis = months:
0. Summary cards: BPV at start, net decisions (purchases − sales), maturities (+ amortisation), drift, BPV at end, duration (if MV available).
1. Portfolio BPV by maturity bucket (stacked bars, month-end, sequential single-hue palette from short to long end).
2. Monthly BPV change decomposition (stacked bars: purchases, sales, maturities, amortisation, drift; distinct colours, fixed legend).
3. Reference rate (and additional series from the configuration) at month-end.
4. Approximate rate effect for the month (bars: gain / loss; caption stating it is an approximation).
5. (If configured) start vs end of year per bucket, and the benchmark.
6. Monthly table below the charts: BPV start, purchases, sales, maturities, amortisation, drift, BPV end, Δrate (bp), rate effect, residual difference from the consistency tests.

Technical requirements:
- Python (pandas, plotly); modular code: separate functions for loading, decomposition, buckets and plotting; the entire config in one dict / YAML file at the top so I can change parameters without touching the code.
- Interactive hover tooltips, readable on both light and dark backgrounds.
- One Y axis per chart (do not mix BPV and % scales), shared X axis across all panels.
- Labels in English, units next to axes.

